What patch 0001 needs to build on a Mac since M156, and still on M158: the simulcast
factory's media constants (rtc_media_base is split since M156), no HAVE_NO_MEDIA branches
(gone since M156), and the network thread in place of webrtc-sdk's worker thread, which
WebRTC no longer had apart from it in M156 and no longer has at all in M158 (the audio
device module is made and driven on that thread).

diff --git a/sdk/BUILD.gn b/sdk/BUILD.gn
index 238da2e7aa..1095b5810f 100644
--- a/sdk/BUILD.gn
+++ b/sdk/BUILD.gn
@@ -960,7 +960,7 @@ if (is_ios || is_mac) {
       deps = [
         ":base_objc",
         ":wrapped_native_codec_objc",
-        "../media:rtc_media_base",
+        "../media:media_constants",
         "../media:rtc_simulcast_encoder_adapter",
       ]
     }
